  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Slalom around the court",
  "description": "The players stand in a line, each with a ball. The first dribbles at high speed through a slalom along one board, around the far end and back through a tighter row of low cones along the other board. The next player starts once the one ahead has passed a few cones.\n\nGo around high cones wide, with body, stick and ball all on the outside – not over or inside the cone. Set low cones closer together for short, quick touches. With lots of players, run two lines at once. Move the cones or add a finish to vary it. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Take your whole body around the cone, not just the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Short steps in the turns, long ones on the straights."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to the blade – look up between the cones."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Do not start until the player ahead is up to speed."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 1,
